{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789922855,"nonce":"xt5FlNV+fyECA1JrU992yYeAou8=","title":"Reading a name nothing assigns to is an Undef read, not a NameError","message":"scimark.main calls time.time() where time is imported only inside the if __name__ block of the module; CPython raises NameError: name 'time' is not defined. zypy fails with 'type mismatch: expected integer, got Undef' from the interpreter, because a name with no assignment anywhere in scope is typed Object and read as an uninitialised variable. The read should raise NameError at run time (a cold path: a zb_fatal with the name), and a call on it should not be lowered as a dynamic attribute call on Undef.","files":null}]}